 "intro_text": "A gloss is an explanatory note or translation that helps a reader understand a word or passage. Glosses are often written in the margin or between the lines of a text. A collection of glosses can form a glossary.\nGlosses were used in medieval biblical and legal commentary and to guide the reading of Classical Chinese texts in Japanese and Korean. In linguistics, a gloss can give the meaning of a word or show the grammatical structure of a passage. In sign-language corpora, identification glosses can serve as consistent labels for signs. In fiction, glosses can interpret passages while also contributing to the narrative.",
 "key": "en/Gloss_(annotation)",
